  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), the Sol-R 5 base alone (no grip) seen from the front and above, front edge at the bottom",
  "mappingSource": "Sol-R 5 Base user manual p.18 \"Mapping\" (https://ts.thrustmaster.com/download/accessories/Manuals/SOL-R/Sol-R_5_BASE_User_Manual.pdf) plus the numbers printed on the base: 1/2 and 3/4 left switches, 5-8 left buttons, 9/10/11 left encoder (11 = push), 12/13 and 14/15 right switches, 16-19 right buttons, 20-23 right 4-position rotary, Slider0 = thrust slider",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "Encoder 9 / 10: the manual and the printed double arrow do not say which turn direction is 9; the catalog cw = 9 / ccw = 10 is not confirmed (press 11 is). Catalog discrepancy: panel.button.1-4 and 12-15 are named \"backlit button\" in the catalog, but per manual p.18 they are the positions of four 2-way SWITCHES (1/2 = left outer switch \"2\", 3/4 = left inner switch \"4\", 14/15 = right inner switch \"15\", 12/13 = right outer switch \"13\"). The manual draws the lower number above the higher one, so up = lower number is assumed (map=medium for the direction). panel.button.20-23 (\"right encoder\") are the four positions of the right rotary selector (labels 20 21 22 23 from left to right), all marked on the knob. panel.axis.1 (Slider0) is the centre THRUST slider, typed \"knob\" in the catalog.",
